Third-party material
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org/) - LGPL-2.1-or-later

   The AMV format has no public specification. Two generated source files in this
   project contain the fixed constant tables that the format requires, extracted
   mechanically from the FFmpeg source tree:

     core/src/com/amvconverter/core/Sp5xTables.java
        generated from libavcodec/sp5x.h
        (the AMV/SP5X quantisation tables and the standard JPEG Annex K Huffman
        tables that every AMV decoder synthesises its JPEG header from)

     core/src/com/amvconverter/core/AdpcmTables.java
        generated from libavcodec/adpcm_data.c
        (the IMA ADPCM step and index tables)

   Both files are regenerated by tools/gen-tables.js and tools/gen-adpcm.js, and
   both carry a header saying so. They are data tables required for
   interoperability, redistributed here with attribution under the terms of the
   GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later.

   No FFmpeg code is compiled, linked, or otherwise included in this project: the
   encoder, decoder, container reader/writer, scaler and Android layer are all
   original implementations.

2. Format research

   docs/research/ contains third-party research and analysis of the AMV format
   written for this project. External claims referenced there belong to their
   respective authors; each source is cited in place.

